54:39.440 --> 54:43.320
Yeah, I'm here today to talk about the culinary

54:43.820 --> 54:47.953
water IFFP update. The update is

54:48.212 --> 54:51.825
from last year's 2025 version,

54:51.938 --> 54:54.594
which was the most recent version.

54:56.728 --> 55:00.009
In in the course of working at Eagle Mountain City,

55:00.123 --> 55:03.922
I've noticed that there's a lot of changes happening in the city. I'm sure

55:04.422 --> 55:08.396
you guys see it too, and change is happening fast. And so because

55:08.444 --> 55:11.927
of some of the changes that have happened, we've felt it was necessary to

55:12.427 --> 55:14.188
take that IFFP and do an update to it.

55:16.009 --> 55:19.322
There are several reasons for that. We'll get into more of the details

55:19.419 --> 55:19.939
here in a minute.

55:23.146 --> 55:26.460
One of the main reasons we started looking at

55:26.960 --> 55:29.871
doing an update to this was a new master plan.

55:31.586 --> 55:35.247
This is for the Talons Cove Spring Run area. Brandon was just talking about

55:35.747 --> 55:39.831
that. We're already getting commercial applications up in that area for

55:40.331 --> 55:44.069
development. You can see Walmart kind of in the lower left

55:44.569 --> 55:48.477
there and SR 73 on the south side of the map. This is

55:48.542 --> 55:52.307
all part of the mine that's up there that Hadco

55:52.807 --> 55:53.546
owns and runs.

55:56.932 --> 56:00.052
The plan is to eventually build this all out with commercial,

56:00.730 --> 56:04.090
institutional, and at this point it's It's all a

56:04.590 --> 56:07.896
master-planned area, but the assumption

56:07.928 --> 56:12.311
was when we did our original IFMP was that this project area was 30

56:12.327 --> 56:15.715
years out or more before they would finish mining in that area and

56:16.215 --> 56:19.905
actually start building. But the reality is we're already getting applications

56:19.953 --> 56:23.534
in for kind of the south end and the west end that's not

56:23.582 --> 56:26.713
part of the mine itself that is part of this master plan. And so we—

56:27.740 --> 56:31.488
We thought, let's take a step back and include this area. It's a large area

56:31.988 --> 56:34.347
of land. Let's include it in our planning for the future.

56:39.512 --> 56:42.727
The next big piece of change was our

56:42.823 --> 56:45.684
SR-73 Central Utah Pipeline.

56:46.664 --> 56:50.190
This is a pipeline— Central Utah actually provides

56:50.206 --> 56:53.523
about half of our culinary water, and we have a contract

56:53.845 --> 56:57.439
to supply a lot more of our culinary water in the

56:57.939 --> 57:01.740
future. Our existing pipeline from central Utah comes up Pony Express

57:02.240 --> 57:05.608
from a pump station down right inside Saratoga

57:06.108 --> 57:09.380
Springs, and that one is basically at capacity at this point.

57:09.877 --> 57:13.216
And so if we want more of the central Utah water that we have contracted,

57:13.456 --> 57:16.907
we need a new pipeline. Now, up on

57:17.407 --> 57:20.968
73, right on the east end of the kind of the blue line there,

57:23.761 --> 57:27.472
Central Utah has a big terminal, what they call their terminal reservoir,

57:28.243 --> 57:32.130
and I think it's 20 million gallons with room for expansion in

57:32.162 --> 57:34.539
that area. They pump water to there,

57:35.391 --> 57:39.310
and then it's the city's responsibility to take the water from there and

57:39.406 --> 57:43.245
get it the rest of the way into the city. And so part

57:43.745 --> 57:47.245
of that project will be a pump station there next to their reservoirs, and then

57:47.919 --> 57:52.398
the The blue line and the purple lines that you see are options for routes

57:52.512 --> 57:55.926
that that pipeline is going to take from that pump station into the city.

57:57.646 --> 58:01.147
As we did our 30% design, those costs came in.

58:01.195 --> 58:04.422
We had a cost in there in the original IFFP, but the

58:04.519 --> 58:07.536
more detailed cost estimate came in higher than we anticipated.

58:08.293 --> 58:12.276
Part of that was because we upsized the pipeline for additional

58:12.646 --> 58:15.946
future growth and the potential for additional Central Utah water if that

58:16.446 --> 58:19.610
ever comes available, so we only have to build this pipeline once and not

58:19.626 --> 58:22.791
have to run parallel lines. So we're we're looking to the future. We're planning for

58:23.291 --> 58:25.951
the future, but because of that, the cost came in higher.

58:30.203 --> 58:34.220
Okay, the other thing is that we have

58:34.943 --> 58:38.429
several wells that are under construction right now. We have

58:38.710 --> 58:40.426
a tank that's under construction.

58:42.014 --> 58:44.747
In the Scarlet Ridge area down south.

58:46.734 --> 58:50.111
And based on the pricing trends that we saw from those bids and

58:50.289 --> 58:53.033
from the contractors coming in and building those,

58:53.960 --> 58:57.727
we realized that the cost for future tanks

58:57.775 --> 59:01.156
and wells in this IFFP were a little on

59:01.656 --> 59:05.249
the low end. And so we decided to bump those up so that

59:05.607 --> 59:08.468
the impact fees that we would collect, which will be based on,

59:08.903 --> 59:13.120
on the IFFP cost estimates, would reflect the

59:13.313 --> 59:14.295
real-world costs.

59:18.882 --> 59:22.968
And then the bottom line for culinary water, and these numbers

59:23.468 --> 59:27.103
are different from what you saw, I think, if you looked at the original PowerPoint

59:27.135 --> 59:31.242
that was attached. I updated these numbers because

59:31.258 --> 59:34.785
they didn't reflect exactly what was in the plans, but these numbers do

59:34.865 --> 59:38.236
reflect now. So we went from about $73.2 million to

59:38.736 --> 59:42.311
$109.1 million just for the culinary water infrastructure over the next

59:42.712 --> 59:47.188
5 years. So that's a big gap, which means

59:47.782 --> 59:51.119
the IFFP update was, was needed for

59:51.151 --> 59:54.456
sure. And the whole point of this

59:54.956 --> 59:58.499
is so that the new growth coming in, they'll pay the impact fees and those

59:58.531 --> 01:00:01.130
