that, I suppose. But one of the— going down

01:26:00.620 --> 01:26:03.485
to the first yellow highlighted item on the left-hand side,

01:26:03.759 --> 01:26:05.561
the leftmost column under provision,

01:26:07.594 --> 01:26:10.855
there is a nonconforming lot threshold

01:26:10.887 --> 01:26:14.165
callout. And then there should

01:26:14.665 --> 01:26:17.786
also be down below that a size minimum for

01:26:17.872 --> 01:26:20.881
lots. One of the key issues in that

01:26:21.381 --> 01:26:24.319
project has been the desire of the residents,

01:26:24.335 --> 01:26:27.838
it sounds like to me, at least of the committee and the HOA, to preserve

01:26:27.951 --> 01:26:31.827
a 5-lot minimum, recognizing there are a few lots that are under that threshold that

01:26:32.327 --> 01:26:35.236
are necessarily grandfathered or legally nonconforming, as we would say,

01:26:36.880 --> 01:26:40.695
and that any future lots that would be derived

01:26:40.711 --> 01:26:43.942
from properties, if there are any ever, from existing

01:26:44.287 --> 01:26:48.401
Platted lots would be at least 5 acres in size and preserve 5 acres

01:26:48.822 --> 01:26:52.667
for the parent property. The contrasting

01:26:53.009 --> 01:26:56.727
ARLL zone suggestion is

01:26:56.825 --> 01:27:00.184
to allow for 3 acres as a minimum,

01:27:01.138 --> 01:27:03.532
and it grandfathers lots under 3 acres.

01:27:06.568 --> 01:27:08.927
And I don't know how much you want me to go over this verbally.

01:27:10.262 --> 01:27:14.057
Or if you want me to let you read, Chair, you might just define that

01:27:14.557 --> 01:27:19.352
for me here. But a couple of callouts that are of note: commercial

01:27:19.852 --> 01:27:23.434
equestrian operations are noted as being a special

01:27:23.934 --> 01:27:26.954
use opportunity in the historic zone,

01:27:27.147 --> 01:27:30.238
I'll call it. And bear in mind, as a reminder,

01:27:30.304 --> 01:27:32.851
which you know, but in case it's needing to be said,

01:27:34.312 --> 01:27:37.656
our special uses in code may or may not yet be

01:27:38.046 --> 01:27:42.189
entered or codified. There are special uses

01:27:42.689 --> 01:27:45.336
that are defined. There's a few standards, and there's some that are maybe referenced but

01:27:45.836 --> 01:27:49.030
aren't— there's no standards given to them. They're basically an

01:27:49.530 --> 01:27:52.483
allowed use as long as you meet these certain standards. They're kind of like the

01:27:52.983 --> 01:27:56.257
conditional use permit became in Utah some years ago versus other cities and

01:27:56.757 --> 01:28:00.401
states— other states, we'll say. Sorry.

01:28:01.541 --> 01:28:04.946
When it comes to the ARL zone, as noted

01:28:05.446 --> 01:28:07.908
