01:28:22.145 --> 01:28:25.697
RLL zone. Now there

01:28:26.197 --> 01:28:30.145
are some business opportunities the RLL zone allows for, adding farm stands

01:28:30.259 --> 01:28:32.411
and separate agricultural sales activities.

01:28:34.750 --> 01:28:38.154
And as it says, a special use path for commercial equestrian operations

01:28:39.905 --> 01:28:40.473
is not there.

01:28:51.299 --> 01:28:54.845
We have a little issue on the ARL zone language.

01:28:55.283 --> 01:28:57.745
It's called out on the top of that That's a column.

01:28:59.430 --> 01:29:03.808
But I wanna skip on down to something of more substance,

01:29:03.872 --> 01:29:07.526
basically. Storage and shipping containers. So the

01:29:08.026 --> 01:29:11.196
historic zone recognizes that there are some out there.

01:29:11.407 --> 01:29:14.975
I don't know how many, I haven't tried to inventory them. At least

01:29:15.072 --> 01:29:19.711
one. And that those can be allowed one

01:29:20.211 --> 01:29:24.159
at a time, looks like, per lot. But in the

01:29:24.659 --> 01:29:27.655
ARL zone, that's omitted as a subsection,

01:29:28.264 --> 01:29:31.231
basically getting your back to just not gonna allow for them.

01:29:32.658 --> 01:29:36.331
And so whatever's there could be grandfathered, and we can— bearing in mind,

01:29:36.844 --> 01:29:40.276
let me back up one quick step, I'm sorry. We have

01:29:40.776 --> 01:29:42.425
a legal nonconforming use section in our code,

01:29:43.804 --> 01:29:46.306
germane to any other city or county pretty much anymore.

01:29:47.508 --> 01:29:48.647
But it's pretty short.

01:29:50.568 --> 01:29:54.015
And at one time the goal was to revamp it,

01:29:54.031 --> 01:29:57.857
to give it a little more meat, if you will. I looked

01:29:58.357 --> 01:30:03.347
at what Provo had and other places. Theirs is pretty long and— excuse

01:30:03.847 --> 01:30:07.600
me— but it has a lot of good stuff to it, in it. But there's

01:30:08.100 --> 01:30:11.304
always been a desire from staff's point of view to make sure that anything

01:30:11.660 --> 01:30:15.522
that's out there that post the adoption of any of these items

01:30:15.554 --> 01:30:19.212
codes or anything else. That where people would like to

01:30:19.485 --> 01:30:23.656
apply for grandfather rights to say, we believe this was legal to begin with and

01:30:24.156 --> 01:30:27.988
we've carried it along all through this, this time period, and now that

01:30:28.488 --> 01:30:31.646
the zoning's changed, we'd like to have it recognized formally as being, quote, grandfathered,

01:30:32.865 --> 01:30:36.331
then we, using what our code is now or something better in the future,

01:30:36.652 --> 01:30:40.021
should be in a position to do that. We need to respect

01:30:40.521 --> 01:30:43.622
people's property rights. And so we would ask for any kind of information that they

01:30:44.122 --> 01:30:47.818
have to give us, and there's a laundry list to give you, like things that

01:30:48.318 --> 01:30:51.301
are commonly used for that. But, but we would then create a record,

01:30:51.753 --> 01:30:56.354
and maybe that's a, in the future, a free application that they go

01:30:56.854 --> 01:31:00.165
for, you know, and file online. But in any event, it would be something to

01:31:00.665 --> 01:31:05.511
protect them and their property rights, whether it's a situation or

01:31:06.011 --> 01:31:09.324
some other nonconformance. And then that's to the best of our knowledge. So if there

01:31:09.357 --> 01:31:12.648
were countervening evidence, it would come forward and we would factor that

01:31:13.148 --> 01:31:16.165
in someday. In any event, that's the goal,

01:31:16.277 --> 01:31:19.970
is to protect those rights. And so now some

01:31:20.470 --> 01:31:23.262
of these things you see being not allowed in one zone, perhaps if they are

01:31:23.762 --> 01:31:26.955
